Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 06:11:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11015/11171] File the exp6968 wrong-gate defect where someone
 will act on it

The defect was recorded in a research note, which is where designs go to be
remembered rather than where bugs go to be fixed. Moving it to known-issues so
it is findable by anyone looking for work.

exp6968 reports failed_check immutable_transition_source. That gate is an
early-return sentinel appended with a hardcoded False when an earlier gate has
already failed, before the transition source is read at all. The real failure
was zero engine_resolution rows upstream. A reader chasing the named gate
investigates transition immutability, which was never involved -- I did, for
several minutes, before reading the source.

Worth its own entry because it is the same class as the conductor's
artifact_not_updated_past_bootstrap, which named the bootstrap path for a
verdict-path rejection and cost an hour on a wrong hypothesis, and which was
fixed yesterday as REQ-CONDUCTOR-VERDICT-3 by splitting the reason. exp6968
wants the same treatment.

Not fixing it now, and saying why: exp6968 cannot succeed until the eval emits
induction_attempts, so improving the error message alone would sharpen the
diagnosis of a failure that should stop occurring. The two belong in one change.

Written on an hourly what-is-not-written-is-forgotten pass, which is what
surfaced that the item was filed in the wrong place.

